  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Complex having maximum number of unpaired electrons will exhibit maximum attraction to applied magnetic field.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>system</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>eg</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>system</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>eg</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>system</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>eg</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>system</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>eg</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons.</p><p>So Option D is correct.</p>"
